name c01m05-double-down
timeout 700
time 1996-03-22T03:00:00Z

# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996), CAMPAIGN ONE, SORTIE 1.5 OF 8 — "DOUBLE DOWN".
# Spec: mods/f22/doc/campaign.md 2. Geometry: mods/f22/doc/terrain.md 3. Substitutions:
# mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md. The five campaign-wide disclosures: c01m01-snake-eyes.fbm.
#
# THE TASK [TXT]: destroy Flight Group `Alpha` so that Viper Squadron can bomb the Nanuchka missile
# boats. Briefed 40 NM SE. TWO measured points, not one [ORF]: the boats at 40.4 NM / 156.2 deg, the
# MiG-29 CAP at 34.0 NM / 158.5 deg. Both are flown; the CAP's point is derived here with terrain.md's
# own constants — 34.0 NM = 62.97 km, dlat = 62.97 cos 158.5 / 111.32 = -0.5263 deg,
# dlon = 62.97 sin 158.5 / (111.32 cos 18.57) = +0.2187 deg -> 18.30451 N / 100.56729 E.
#
# THERE IS NO WATER AND THERE ARE NO SHIPS, AND THIS IS THE CAMPAIGN'S WORST MISMATCH.
#   terrain.md 6: the boats' computed point is 205 km from the nearest documented reach of the real
#   Mekong, in the Nan/Phrae uplands where there is no navigable water of any kind — and the manual's
#   own ship entry is a Nanuchka-III CORVETTE with two triple SS-N-9 launchers, a seagoing warship.
#   The fiction was already implausible before anybody anchored it. Not patched (terrain.md 6's
#   decision, taken the same way as in sortie 1.3: keep the measured point).
#   FlightBox HAS NO SHIP MODULE AT ALL — no hull, no naval movement, no SS-N-9, no anti-ship weapon.
#   The substitute is `target_soft` x 2, 300 m apart, sitting on the 0 m plane: a stationary object
#   that can be bombed. WHAT IS THEREBY NOT MEASURED, in full: the boats do not move, do not radiate,
#   do not shoot back, and the whole reason a Nanuchka is dangerous is absent. `target_soft` and not
#   `target_hard` because a corvette is a thin-hulled ship and the catalogue's hard class describes a
#   bunker — see mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md for the rule applied to all five ground objects.
#
# SUBSTITUTIONS OTHERWISE
#   Flight Group Alpha (MiG-29 CAP) -> `mig29` x 2. EXACT.
#   Viper Squadron -> `f16` x 2 with `mk84`. Viper flies F-16s in the fiction too [TXT]; what is
#     substituted is only the weapon (GBU-30 JDAM -> mk84, the campaign-wide rule and its measurement
#     are in c01m03-luckiest-man-in-laos.fbm).
#
# WHY VIPER RUNS IN 20 km SHORT AND NOT 45, AND WHY THAT INVERTS THE FICTION'S CAUSALITY. The
# briefing says Storm destroys Alpha SO THAT Viper can bomb. `FBMissionRunner` ends the whole run at
# the FIRST physical K.O. of any unit, covered or not — and 2 x `f16` against 2 x `mig29` with R-27R
# is a fight Blue can lose. MEASURED on this file at a 45 km Viper spawn: `s5lead` combat-ineffective
# at t = 91.8 s, the run over, both boats INTACT, and the sortie's whole second half unmeasured. Viper
# now releases at ~t = 72 s, before the air fight can end the run. THE CONSEQUENCE IS STATED, NOT
# HIDDEN: the strike no longer waits on the escort, so this file cannot show that clearing Alpha was
# what MADE the bomb run possible. It shows the two things separately. That is an ENGINE limit — a
# mission cannot contain a losing air fight followed by anything at all — and it is the same
# `FirstFlightKo` constraint mods/f16/src/missions/w2-06-escort.fbm records from the other side.
#
# THE TWO CONDITIONS ARE DECLARED SEPARATELY SO THAT THE TWO FAILURES STAY DISTINGUISHABLE, which is
# campaign.md's own reading rule for this sortie ("they fail for opposite reasons"):
#   `s5lead`   kill s5a1, kill s5a2, protect unit s5vip1, survive   <- Storm's own job AND the escort
#   `s5vip1`   kill s5bt1, survive                                  <- the bomb run
#   `s5vip2`   kill s5bt2, survive
# A run in which Alpha survives shows up as `s5lead`'s unmet `kill`; a run in which Alpha dies and
# Viper dies anyway shows up as `s5lead`'s VIOLATED `protect` — different lines, different units,
# never the same number.
#
# READING RULE (binding). Two verdicts, both required, and they must be read as a pair.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 = `s5lead` SUCCESS (both Fulcrums dead, Viper lead alive, Storm Leader alive) AND
#   `s5vip1`/`s5vip2` SUCCESS (both boats destroyed).
#   `s5lead` FAIL with `protect unit s5vip1 state=violated` = Viper was shot: the mission failed at the
#   escort, not at the bomb run, EVEN IF Alpha died first. Report it that way.
#   `s5lead` TIMEOUT with a `kill` unmet = Alpha survived: the mission failed before the bomb run
#   became relevant.
#   `s5lead` FAIL with `protect` MET and the two `kill`s unmet = Storm LOST the air fight while Viper
#   lived. That is the outcome this file measures today (see below); it is a mission loss and it says
#   nothing about the bomb run, which succeeded in the same run.
#   `s5vip*` TIMEOUT with `kill unit s5bt*` unmet while both Viper aircraft live = the WEAPON did not
#   reach the target, which is the sortie's third possible cause and the one c01m03 measures in
#   detail. Do not merge it with either of the other two.

# MEASURED (exit 1): THE BOMB RUN WORKS AND THE ESCORT DOES NOT.
#   t = 86.3 / 86.7 s   both `target_soft` boats DESTROYED, `mk84` CCRP, structure destroyed
#   t = 91.7 s          `s5lead` combat-ineffective to the MiG-29 pair; `FirstFlightKo` ends the run
#   verdict             s5vip1/s5vip2 SUCCESS, s5two SUCCESS, s5lead FAIL, both `kill unit s5a*` unmet
#   THE CAUSE, NAMED: two `f16` with AIM-120 do not beat two `mig29` with R-27R on a head-on 60 km
#   merge in this tree. That is a doctrine/airframe result, not a defect, and it is the same pairing
#   mods/f16/src/missions/duel-fulcrum-high.fbm grades on purpose.

unit s5lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm5 1
  spawn 18.80599 100.35892 5000 158.5 480     # 60 km up-track of the CAP point — see the header
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 18.30451 100.56729 5000 480              # the CAP point [ORF] 34.0 NM / 158.5 deg from Tyler
  objective kill unit s5a1
  objective kill unit s5a2
  objective protect unit s5vip1
  objective survive

unit s5two
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm5 2
  spawn 18.80105 100.34568 5000 158.5 480     # 1.5 km across track from the leader
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 18.30451 100.56729 5000 480
  objective protect unit s5vip2
  objective survive

unit s5vip1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight viper5 1
  spawn 18.38022 100.55829 900 156.2 450      # 20 km short of the boats, low — see the header
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 18.21583 100.63465 900 450               # ITS aim point: the northern boat
  wp 18.06789 100.70332 900 450               # egress 18 km beyond
  objective kill unit s5bt1
  objective survive

unit s5vip2
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight viper5 2
  spawn 18.37478 100.54530 900 156.2 450      # 1.5 km across track from Viper lead
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 18.21692 100.63725 900 450               # ITS aim point: the southern boat, 300 m away
  wp 18.06789 100.70332 900 450
  objective kill unit s5bt2
  objective survive

unit s5a1
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 18.30451 100.56729 5000 338.5 450     # AT the measured CAP point, inbound up the track
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 7 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 18.97315 100.28933 5000 450
  objective survive

unit s5a2
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 18.30945 100.58050 5000 338.5 450     # 1.5 km across track from its leader
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 7 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 18.97315 100.28933 5000 450
  objective survive

unit s5bt1
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 18.21583 100.63465 ground 156.2 0     # "Nanuchka", northern

unit s5bt2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 18.21692 100.63725 ground 156.2 0     # "Nanuchka", southern, 300 m away
